      "content": "Your symptoms could indeed be related to stress, as tension often manifests as a dull ache in the jaw and neck due to chronic clenching or poor posture. However, a bad tooth infection or other dental issues can also cause similar deep aches that radiate through the jaw and neck. It's wise to monitor if the pain becomes sharper or worsens during certain activities before deciding whether to see a dentist or a doctor.",
